								SI demonstrates a pronounced upward trajectory with chronological age (5.61 m/s &rarr; 12.80 m/s), whereas RI exhibits non-monotonic behavior, highlighting that structural wall stiffness and real-time vasomotor tone are physiologically decoupled.
